          "text": "Headache"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent occipital/temporal pressure headache for 1–2 weeks, up to 6/10, worse on getting out of bed or bending; lasts minutes to 1 hour and settles with rest or Panadol. Mild nausea. No photophobia, phonophobia, aura, or focal neurology."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
